gdoc v2.10.0 is published and this is v2.9.0. `gdoc update` installs it.

gdoc v2.9.0

Usage: gdoc <command> [words] [flags]

  auth status  Say whether gdoc has a token, when it expires, and what it may reach.
  auth login   Print the Google sign-in URL and wait for the browser to come back.
  read         Print the document as text, with the ids a comment or a suggestion is named by.
  comments     List the comment threads with their ranges, their replies and the next cursor.
  suggestions  List the suggestions pending in the document.
  export       Write the document into the hub as Markdown, one file per tab, with its pictures beside it.
  restyle      Survey a document against the house style, or apply that style where the document stands.
  probe        Create a throwaway document and say whether Docs honours a suggestion today.
  reply        Write one reply into a comment thread, under the robot prefix.
  propose      Propose changes as native suggestions, each with the comment that says why.
  withdraw     Take back one pending suggestion, and only one gdoc proposed itself.
  annotate     Leave a comment on the exact words you quote, under the robot prefix, changing nothing.
  build        Build the note as a house-style docx on this machine, with no network at all.
  publish      Build the note as a house-style document and upload it into one folder.
  update       Replace this gdoc with the newest release, or say what one would take.
  mcp          Serve gdoc to Claude Desktop over stdin and stdout, as a protocol session rather than one object.
  help         Print every command gdoc takes, or the words and flags of one.
  completion   Write the completion script for one shell, and say the line that turns it on.

Run gdoc help <command> for the words and flags one takes.
